    "body": "Problem:\nWith 'cmdheight' 0, ui2 sets 'cmdheight' to 1 when the cmdline is shown, using\n'splitkeep' = \"screen\" to keep the text in place. When the cursor is on the\nlast visible line of the window, 'splitkeep' moves the cursor up instead\n(documented behavior, see Test_splitkeep_cmdheight) and adds a jumplist entry.\nThis happens for any cmdline, even `:<Esc>`, and the cursor is not moved back.\nvim.lsp.buf.rename() reads the cursor after input() returns, so it renames the\nwrong symbol.\n\nSolution:\nChange 'cmdheight' with :keepjumps, and restore the cursor if it was moved, so\nthe window scrolls by one line instead. The text still stays in place when the\ncursor is not at the bottom.\n\nFixes #42496\n",
